How the reference pictures align with the target video — Picture 1 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video.

integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Continuous shot of the old scientist SITTING ON THE CONCRETE FLOOR, slumped with his back against the steel control desk, legs stretched out, lit by the green panel light. The camera stays still and slightly above him. Start exactly at Picture 1. He stays seated on the floor the whole time and never rises, leans forward or stands. For the first three and a half seconds he speaks a short sentence in Japanese in a weak, rasping whisper, his lips moving slowly, a faint knowing smile at the end. Then he lets out a long last breath, his eyes slowly close, and his head sinks gently sideways against the desk and stays still; his gloved hands rest limp on the floor. No blood, no wound visible. No text appears. Keep the dark blue-green color grade.

overall_soundscape: His weak rasping whisper, a long last exhale, then only the low hum of machinery.

non_diegetic_music: N/A
